tive stress genes, and heart rate variability in an elderly cohort</article-title><source>Environ Health Perspect</source><volume>115</volume><fpage>1617</fpage><lpage>1622</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18007994</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b7-ehp-117-a340b"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Dolinoy</surname><given-names>DC</given-names></name><name><surname>Jirtle</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Environmental epigenomics in human health and disease</article-title><source>Environ Mol Mutagen</source><volume>49</volume><issue>1</issue><fpage>4</fpage><lpage>8</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18172876</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b8-ehp-117-a340b"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jirtle</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name><name><surname>Skinner</surname><given-names>MK</given-names></name></person-group><year>2007</year><article-title>Environmental epigenomics and disease susceptibility</article-title><source>Nat Rev</source><volume>8</volume><issue>4</issue><fpage>253</fpage><lpage>262</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b9-ehp-117-a340b"><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Tarantini</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Bonzini</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Apostoli</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Pegoraro</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Bollati</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Marinelli</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2009</year><article-title>Effects of particulate matter on genomic DNA methylation content and <italic>iNOS</italic> promoter methylation</article-title><source>Environ Health Perspect</source><vo